{"name":"Marigold","hex":"#fcc006","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Marigold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rubber glove, especially one for use in household cleaning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Marigold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marigold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Marigold is a yellow-orange color. It is named after the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/French_marigold.jpg/330px-French_marigold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marigold_(color)","wikidata":"Q19572932"},{"title":"Calendula","blocks":[{"text":"Calendula is a genus of about 15–20 species of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the daisy family, Asteraceae that are often known as marigolds. They are native to Europe, North Africa, Macaronesia, West Asia and Western Himalayas and have their center of diversity in the Mediterranean Region. Other plants known as marigolds include corn marigold, desert marigold, marsh marigold, and plants of the genus Tagetes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg/330px-Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calendula","wikidata":"Q147281"},{"title":"Marigold (2007 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Marigold is a 2007 romantic musical comedy directed by Willard Carroll. The film is about Marigold Lexton, an American actress who begins a personal transformation and becomes enamored with India as she experiences Bollywood firsthand. It stars Salman Khan and Ali Larter as the title character."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Marigoldfilmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","li